  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "getNextTLVRecord",
    "file": "PcapPlusPlus/Packet++/header/TLVData.h",
    "description": "TLVRecordReader::getNextTLVRecord() validates that the current record ends within the TLV buffer, but after assigning the following record it only checks whether that record's declared size is zero. It does not verify that the newly returned record, including its header and declared total size, fits in the remaining TLV buffer. Consequently NflogLayer::getTlvByType() can accept a truncated NFULA_PAYLOAD TLV with an attacker-controlled oversized recordLen. NflogLayer::parseNextLayer() derives payloadLen from that unvalidated length and creates an IPv4Layer whose logical m_DataLen extends beyond the RawPacket allocation; getDstIPv4Address() then performs the reported 4-byte out-of-bounds read.",
    "conditions": "The harness writes the fuzz bytes as a pcap, PcapFileReaderDevice copies the captured packet into a caplen-sized heap allocation, and Packet parses its NFLOG link-layer data. The NFLOG TLV sequence must contain at least one traversable preceding TLV followed by an NFULA_PAYLOAD record (type 9) whose declared recordLen exceeds the bytes remaining in the captured packet. The payload bytes must look sufficiently like IPv4 for IPv4Layer::isDataValid() (version 4, IHL at least 5, and a declared/derived payload length of at least sizeof(iphdr)); the actual capture is truncated before the destination-address field. The unchecked next-TLV length makes isPacketOfType(IPv4) succeed and the harness's destination-address accessor reads past the caplen allocation."
  },
